{[%evp 0,38,27,22,13,0,43,46,46,46,19,40,47,50,44,51,51,52,52,49,63,68,71,71,82,84,105,123,136,136,123,83,145,107,127,117,123,109,107,104,85]} 1. d4 d5 2. c4 dxc4 {To be honest, only the match day I decided to play QGA. Checking his games I realized he always enters the same positions which seemed quite drawish} 3. Nf3 Nf6 4. e3 e6 5. Bxc4 c5 6. O-O a6 7. dxc5 Bxc5 8. Qxd8+ Kxd8 9. b3 Ke7 10. Bb2 {out from here I was on my own} Rd8 {played after 16 minutes of thinking. I don't think I spent most of my time here on "searching" the right move but rather getting into atmosphere. Until here I was blitzing out the opening moves. The idea of my move was to "wait and see" where my opponent develops his Knight.} ({In fact, I had a file where} 10... Nbd7 {was mentioned. But I simply had no enough time to check all in wider details.} 11. Nbd2 (11. Rd1 b6 12. Nc3 Bb7 13. Na4 Bd6 $132) 11... b6 $5 (11... b5 {often runs under a4}) 12. Rfd1 Bb7 $11 {Followed by bringing the rooks to the open files with equality.}) (10... b5 11. Be2 Bb7 12. a4 b4 13. Nbd2 {with weak c4-square didn't seem convincing}) 11. Be2 $5 {most principled and smart. Delaying b1-Knights development} ({On} 11. Nc3 {I was planning to go} b5 $5 {since after a4 later, I'd have ...-b4 and rerouting Knight to c4 will take some time} 12. Be2 Bb7 13. a4 b4 14. Nb1 Ne4 $40) ({In case of} 11. Nbd2 {I'd go I'd go} b6 {[%cal Gc8b7]}) 11... Bd7 {too slow. I just wasn't convinced about my position already} (11... b6 12. a3 (12. Nc3 Nbd7 13. Na4 Bd6) 12... Bb7 (12... a5 {didn't look convincing either} 13. Nc3 Nbd7 14. Na4 Bd6 15. Nd4 Bb7 16. Rac1 Rac8 17. Nb5 $36) 13. b4 Bd6 14. Nbd2 {[%cal Gd2c4] I wasn't happy about this position}) 12. Rc1 ({On} 12. Nbd2 {I was thinking of I was thinking of} Bb5) ({Engine line:} 12. Nc3 Be8 13. Rac1 Nc6 14. Na4 Bb4 15. Nc5 Na5 16. Nd3 Bd6 17. Rfd1 Rac8) 12... b6 13. Ne5 Ra7 14. a4 Rc7 15. a5 Rcc8 (15... Bd6 16. Rxc7 (16. Nc4 bxa5 17. Nxd6 Rxc1+ 18. Bxc1 Kxd6) 16... Bxc7 17. axb6 Bxb6) 16. h3 {looked slow} ({meanwhile} 16. axb6 Bxb6 17. Nc3 {was giving White huge advantage} (17. Ba3+ Ke8 18. Nc4 Bc7 {Black stays in the game}) 17... Bc7 18. Nxd7 Nfxd7 (18... Rxd7 19. Na4 $18) 19. Ne4 Be5 20. Ba3+ Ke8 21. Nd6+ Bxd6 22. Bxd6 $16 {and White has massive initiative thanks to monstrous Bishops}) 16... Bb4 $1 {going for simplifications!} 17. axb6 Rxc1+ 18. Bxc1 Bb5 $1 19. Bxb5 (19. Bf3 Nfd7 20. Nxd7 Nxd7 21. Ba3 Bxa3 22. Nxa3 Bd3 (22... Nxb6 23. Nxb5 axb5 24. Ra5 $16) 23. b7 Ne5 24. Nc4 Bxc4 25. bxc4 Rb8 26. Rxa6 Nxf3+ 27. gxf3 Rxb7 {and Black should be able holding this Rook ending}) 19... Rd1+ (19... axb5 $4 20. Ra7+ $18) 20. Bf1 Rxc1 21. Nd3 Bc3 $1 {This might be the move my opponent overlooked by letting me play 16...-Bb4} 22. Nxc1 Bxa1 23. Nd3 (23. Nd2 {[%cal Gd2c4] is what I expected more, bringing Knight on c4} Kd7 24. Nc4 Kc6 25. g4 {White has slightly better chances but I was already confident that I'll hold this endgame} Nd5 26. Bg2 Nd7) 23... Kd6 24. Na3 Nfd7 25. Nc4+ Kc6 26. Be2 Nxb6 27. Nde5+ Bxe5 28. Nxe5+ Kc5 29. Nxf7 Kb4 30. Bd1 $6 {now Black takes the initiative} (30. Ng5 e5 31. Ne6 a5 32. Bd1 Na6 $132 {[%cal Gb6d7,Ga6c5]}) 30... N8d7 (30... N6d7 {is even better according to the engine}) 31. Nd8 Nc5 32. Nc6+ Kc3 33. Na5 Kb4 34. Nc6+ Kc3 35. Na5 Kb4 $2 ({It was even "smarter" to go for I should have continued the game with It was even "smarter" to go for} 35... Nd5 {after repeating moves once (since I'm having clear initiative getting couple moves closer to the time control favors me) however, being seriously worse for the most part of the game (especially in KO format tournament) affected on me and I was sort of happy of getting a draw.} 36. Kf1 (36. Bg4) (36. g4 Nb4 37. Kg2 Nbd3 38. Kf3 Nc1 39. Kf4 N1xb3 40. Bxb3 Nxb3 41. Nc6) 36... Nb4 {followed by ...-Nbd3 and ...-Nc1 followed by ... -Nbd3 and ... -Nc1} 37. Ke2 Nbd3 38. Kf3 Kd2 (38... Nc1 39. Nc6 N1xb3 40. Bxb3 Nxb3 41. Ke4 a5 (41... Kc4 42. Ke5 Kc5 43. Nd4 Nxd4 44. exd4+ Kc4 45. f4 $1 a5 46. f5 exf5 47. d5 a4 48. d6 a3 49. d7 a2 50. d8=Q a1=Q+ 51. Kxf5 $11) 42. Nxa5 Nxa5 43. Ke5 Kd2 44. Kxe6 Ke2 45. Kf7 Kxf2 46. Kxg7 Kxe3 47. Kxh7 Kf4 48. Kg6 Kg3 49. Kg5 Nb7 50. h4 Nd6 51. h5 Nf7+ 52. Kg6 Kg4 $11) 39. b4 $8 Kxd1 40. bxc5 Nxc5 {with difficult times for White} 41. h4 Kd2 42. g4 Kc3 43. Kf4 Nd3+ $19) 1/2-1/2

