{[%evp 0,26,28,26,26,28,28,16,16,14,8,6,6,7,21,21,26,26,26,11,11,11,26,25,25,33,35,43,74]} 1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bc4 {Playing Italian against my Italian opponent!} Bc5 4. d3 Nf6 5. O-O O-O 6. Nc3 $5 {Objectively 6.Nc3 kind-moves are not really dangerous for Black, but since it's not been investigated deeply, I wanted to give it a try.} h6 {is being played to prevent Bg5.} ({In case of} 6... d6 {White can also do} 7. Na4 $5 {going after Black's c5-Bishop.}) 7. Be3 $5 {Typical idea. By trading off the Bishops on e3 square White wants to open up the f-file.} Bxe3 (7... Bb6 $5 {is an alternative for Black.}) 8. fxe3 d6 {Black is ready to play ...-Na5} 9. d4 exd4 (9... Na5 10. Be2 $14) ({After} 9... Bg4 $5 10. h3 Bh5 11. Qd3 Re8 $11 {Black's Bishop on h5 is well placed and their position is solid.}) 10. exd4 Nxe4 $5 {This move is tempting. Black wants to simplify the position and get a sound position.} 11. Nxe4 d5 12. Bd3 dxe4 13. Bxe4 {After Black's 10...-Nxe4 more or less all was forced until here. Now Black has a wide choice.} Ne7 $6 {Most natural, but a bit passive.} (13... Re8 {is much more principle. In case of} 14. Bxc6 bxc6 15. Qd3 Qd5 {Black looks comfortable.} 16. c4 (16. Ne5 $6 c5 $17) 16... Bf5 17. Qc3 Qd6 $11) 14. Ne5 $1 {grabbing more space in the center} f6 (14... c6 $2 15. c3 $16 {followed by Bc2-Qd3, Black's in a serious trouble here.}) 15. Nc4 {an interesting choice but perhaps not the best one} (15. Nf3 $5 {was much better according to the engine. White has provoked ...-f6 and now can return back home, just in the style of AlphaZero.}) 15... c6 (15... Be6 $1 {could have solved Black's opening problems.} 16. Na5 Bd5 $1 {Black temporarily sacrifices a pawn but soon will get it back.} 17. Nxb7 Qb8 18. Nc5 Bxe4 19. Nxe4 Qxb2 $11 {and the game should end in a draw}) 16. c3 {stabilizing the center.} Be6 17. Bd3 Kh8 18. Qf3 Qc7 19. Rae1 {Now that all my pieces are concentrated in the center, I must start thinking about how to create an attack on rivalry King.} Bg8 20. Ne3 Rae8 ({fearless engines offer} 20... Bxa2 $5 {but after} 21. c4 {I doubt anyone would consider here} f5 $1 {and apparently Black's OK... Sure...:)}) 21. Qh5 Bh7 $4 {This simply loses on the spot} 22. Bxh7 Kxh7 23. Ng4 $1 {and Black cannot prevent the Rxf6 threat} Qd7 24. Rxf6 $1 {It was a total shocker for my opponent. He believed his position was already fine, and his assessment would be correct if only not this beautiful move!} Nd5 25. Rxe8 Rxf6 26. h3 Rf7 27. Qe5 {Black resigned here. Perhaps he could have yet continued fighting but the position was theoretically lost already.} 1-0

